Translation patch: `value::convert` (mod.rs): btoi, regex and std calls go through `trusted`

Change: `btoi(&*bytes)` becomes `trusted::btoi_<ty>(&*bytes)` (the `impl_from_value_num!` macro takes the helper name as a second argument), `btou(..)` becomes `trusted::btou_u32`/`btou_u8` (the type the call was inferred at), `RE.is_match(bytes)` becomes `trusted::<re>(bytes)` (the regex statics move to trusted.rs), `from_utf8` becomes `trusted::str_from_utf8`, `f.parse::<f32/f64>()` becomes `trusted::str_parse_f32/f64`, `f64::from(x: f32)` (`x.into()`) becomes `trusted::f32_to_f64`, `String::from_utf8(b)` with `e.into_bytes()` becomes `trusted::string_from_utf8` (which returns the bytes as its error), `Duration::new`/`as_secs`/`subsec_nanos` become `trusted::duration_*`, `x.to_string().into()` (i128/u128) becomes `trusted::string_into_bytes(trusted::i128_to_string(x))`, `String::into_bytes` becomes `trusted::string_into_bytes`, and in `From<&str> for Value`, `String::from(x).into_bytes()` becomes `trusted::str_as_bytes(x).to_vec()`. `Ok`/`Err` matches on the replaced calls become `Some`/`None` matches.
Why: Aeneas cannot translate these dependency functions (see patch 40).
Behaviour: Identical: each helper is the call it replaces; where a helper returns `.ok()` only `Ok`/`Err` was observed (and `Option::unwrap` panics exactly where `Result::unwrap` did); `.to_string().into()` (`From<String> for Vec<u8>`) is `into_bytes`; `String::from(x).into_bytes()` and `x.as_bytes().to_vec()` are the same bytes.
Panic message (found in review): where the replaced `btou(..).unwrap()` is now `Option::unwrap` on the helper's result, the panic condition is identical but the message changes from `called Result::unwrap() on an Err value: ParseIntegerError{..}` to `called Option::unwrap() on a None value`.

